#====================================================================
# E543 draft — filled by adaptation run (libasd 1.5.6, OHOS PC)
#====================================================================
id:                     E543
trigger_tool:           clang|cmake|ctest
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        __libcpp_random_is_valid_inttype|IntType must be a supported integer type
severity:               3
category:               portability, libc, cmake
match_keywords:         uniform_int_distribution, libc++, char, static_assert, random, test, OHOS
title:                  Widen uniform_int_distribution to int for narrow integer types on libc++
root_cause:             libc++ enforces the [rand.req.dist] IntType requirements with a static_assert (__libcpp_random_is_valid_inttype): only short, int, long, long long and their unsigned variants are valid, so char, signed char, unsigned char and char8_t are rejected at compile time. libstdc++ accepts char, so upstream code or tests instantiating std::uniform_int_distribution<char> compile with GCC/libstdc++ but fail on the OHOS SDK libc++ with "static assertion failed ... IntType must be a supported integer type".
affected_scope:         C++ code or test suites instantiating uniform_int_distribution with char-family types; every libc++ platform (OHOS SDK, macOS) when cross-checking upstream suites that pass on libstdc++
verification_cmd:       printf '#include <random>\nstd::uniform_int_distribution<char> d(0, 9);\nint main(){}' > t.cpp && clang++ -std=c++11 -stdlib=libc++ t.cpp
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           widen-distribution-and-cast-back
rec_description:        Replace uniform_int_distribution<T> with uniform_int_distribution<int> for types narrower than int, construct it over [numeric_limits<T>::min(), numeric_limits<T>::max()], and static_cast<T>(distro(rng)); keep T itself when sizeof(T) >= sizeof(int). The value range and test semantics are unchanged on both libstdc++ and libc++.
rec_command:            sed-level edit in the affected test/template source; verify with the project test suite (ctest --output-on-failure)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conditional-distribution-type-via-std-conditional
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      document-platform-limit-and-skip
fallback_description:   If editing upstream sources is not allowed for the affected version, record the compile failure as a platform limitation with the static_assert excerpt instead of deleting the test case or swapping the standard library.
fallback_command:       keep the failing TU out of the run only with an explicit documented exclusion list
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          evidence-kept-partial
forbid_1_pattern:       -stdlib=libstdc\+\+|force.*libstdc\+\+
forbid_1_reason:        Swapping the OHOS SDK libc++ for libstdc++ masks the conformance issue and breaks the target platform ABI.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package builds against an unshipped toolchain configuration and fails in clean CI.
forbid_2_pattern:       delete.*test|remove.*test_case.*random
forbid_2_reason:        Removing the affected assertions hides real coverage loss.
forbid_2_consequence:   The upstream suite reports a smaller static denominator without justification.
principles:             P002,P003
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             E321
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E543-draft-E961.md
last_updated:           2026-09-05
source_event:           libasd 1.5.6 OHOS upstream Boost.Test run (test_read_binary_as / test_write_as_binary)
authors:                wanderlust_0823
